[EXPERIMENT A] API Comparison: RDD vs DataFrame vs Dataset
Task: Filter records where totalTasks > 500 and compute average queueWaitMs
  - Spark RDD API       :   285 ms (Legacy, High serialization overhead)
  - Spark Dataset API   :   195 ms (Typed, Encoder overhead)
  - Spark DataFrame API :   373 ms (Untyped, Tungsten optimized)
  Conclusion: DataFrames leverage Tungsten memory & Catalyst optimizer for best speeds.

[EXPERIMENT B] Partition Tuning: Default vs Optimized
Task: Force a massive shuffle via groupBy and count
  - Under-partitioned (2)   :   126 ms (Stragglers/OOM risk)
  - Over-partitioned (200)  :   442 ms (Scheduling overhead)
  - Optimized Tuning (10)   :   113 ms (Balanced task distribution)

